Copyright 2026 Pratik M. Tambe <enthusiasticgeek@gmail.com> and The vani-galois Authors

Generic GF(2^m) finite-field arithmetic and a binary BCH codec built on
top of it, extracted for Dhruva OS's (https://github.com/enthusiasticgeek/dhruvaos)
DharaFS NAND-FTL work (real per-page error-correction with configurable
strength) as a standalone, hardware-agnostic, reusable kosh package --
the field degree and primitive polynomial are caller-supplied parameters,
not hardcoded to any one consumer's specific field, unlike e.g. vani-aes's
deliberately AES-specific GF(2^8) arithmetic.

